      "writtenOn": "2021-06-25T10:57:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "for java_library platform_apis: property means:\n\n\"\"\"\nplatform_apis bool, Whether to compile against the platform APIs instead of an SDK. If true, then sdk_version must be empty. The value of this field is ignored when module\u0027s type isn\u0027t android_app.\n\"\"\"\n\nDevs are probably more used to this definition of \"platform_apis\". Maybe worth renaming the new property to uses_android_non_updatable_apis or something like that?\n\nBut again, sounds like if we added a bootclasspath_fragment for android-non-updtaable stuff, it would make it more consistent?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "7d5300104defd53969fb4ecc282e541f63f562e0",
