        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-25T11:50:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using a bcpf won\u0027t work as outlined in my other comment.\n\nFinding a good name for that property is tricky. It actually adds dependencies on android-non-updatable stubs. However, that name is not quite accurate, e.g. it does not include i18n which is not updatable. It is actually the \"not-provided-by-an-apex\" library.\n\nHow about uses_apis_not_provided_by_an_apex?\nOr a little more succinct uses_non_apex_apis?",
      "parentUuid": "610b5753_80d690d5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "7d5300104defd53969fb4ecc282e541f63f562e0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "53b8bc33_a117b7d3",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061164
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-25T12:39:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Naming is tricky... It doesn\u0027t help that \"updatable\" is overloaded: it may mean actually updatable apexes, or just being part of the mainline program.\n\n- uses_non_apex_apis -- doesn\u0027t read right to me on the first glance. Does APEX provide apis? Are there APIs meant for APEXes? etc.\n- uses_apis_not_provided_by_an_apex - is technically correct (especially if you add _boot_jar suffix), but not succinct.. and I imagine we would want devs to use this flag themselves (not just us setting the values on this once in a while).\n\nI would personally still prefer being consistent with naming in StubLibraries.bp that generate the stubs. It\u0027s unfortunate that its ambiguous there too, but that\u0027s a separate problem. And this property you are adding is meant to signify whether those stubs are included or not, so it\u0027s easier to explain and codesearch I think. So, something like uses_android-non-updatable-stub-sources is fine by me.",
      "parentUuid": "4d59e49a_125b6d81",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "7d5300104defd53969fb4ecc282e541f63f562e0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "15e20d8f_e6fe63bc",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-25T13:38:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, so what I am going to do is pretend that \"android-non-updatable\" is a java_sdk_library. It is not but it creates stub libraries as if they were. So, a bootclasspath_fragment would add the following instead of the uses.... property.\n\nadditional_stubs: [\n    \"android-non-updatable\",\n],\n\nI will map that to the correct libraries under the covers.\n\nLonger term, we will probably need a java_sdk_library_merge module type which can create a single java_sdk_library from multiple libraries and sources. To replace all the repetitive boiler plate in http://cs/android/frameworks/base/StubLibraries.bp?l\u003d238. That can be used to create an android-non-updatable java_sdk_library which will allow the Soong code to be simplified and won\u0027t require modifications to the existing usages.\n\nWDYT of the \"additional_stubs\" property name?",
      "parentUuid": "53b8bc33_a117b7d3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "7d5300104defd53969fb4ecc282e541f63f562e0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8879b9a5_62d7668b",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
