      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-25T15:18:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I like that it\u0027s more declarative. Stubs means it\u0027s a non static dependency, and is used for compile only. It also lists actual java_library names that define the stubs, so it\u0027s more discoverable.\n\nIt\u0027s unfortunate that we have fragments: dependency and then additional_stubs: dependency for pretty much the same thing (at least from devs perspective), but oh well...",
